    "evidence_text": "PolyResponse: A Rank-based Approach to Task-Oriented Dialogue with Application in Restaurant Search and Booking\tWe present PolyResponse, a conversational search engine that supports task-oriented dialogue.\n\nThe PolyResponse engine is trained on hundreds of millions of examples extracted from real conversations: it learns what responses are appropriate in different conversational contexts.\n\nRelying on non-generative response retrieval we describe the PolyResponse conversational search engine and its application in the task of restaurant search and booking.\n\nDue to its retrieval-based design, with the PolyResponse engine there is no need to engineer a structured ontology, or to solve\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Text Representation.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Photo Representation.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Data Source 1: Reddit.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Data Source 2: Yelp.\n\nTraining of the multi-modal sub-network then maximises the similarity of captions encoded with the response encoder $h_r$ to the photo representation $h_p$.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Index of Responses.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: PolyResponse in a Nutshell.\n\nSpeech-to-text and text-to-speech conversion in the PolyResponse system is currently supported by the off-the-shelf Google Cloud tools.",
